# Central tendency and variability summary

Per-design-cell log-χ geometric means and variance components (`f_ratio`, `abs_TF_ratio`, `PGA_ratio`, `PSA_ratio`, `Ia_ratio`) from `join_master.h5`.

- Design cells: **243** (`Vs1`, `Height`, `CoV`, `rH`, `aHV`)
- Within cell: **101** nodes × **100** seeds
- Non-positive / non-finite χ values are dropped before taking logs
- Primary variances use population moments (ddof = 0); `*_ddof1` columns in `cell_summary.csv` use sample moments (ddof = 1)

## Output files

| File | Rows | Contents |
|------|-----:|----------|
| `cell_summary.csv` | one per cell × metric (243 × 5 = 1215) | Design factors, overall geomean $G$, log-mean, linear mean/median, rms components $s_W$, $s_\mu$, $s_B$, $s_\nu$, $s_{\mathrm{total}}$, fractions, naive-sum diagnostic, interaction residual, P10–P90 of seed/node geomeans, `decomp_ok` |
| `within_per_seed.csv` | one per cell × metric × seed | Per-seed log-mean $\mu_j$, geomean $G^{\mathrm{seed}}_j = e^{\mu_j}$, within-seed variance $s^{2}_{W,j}$ and $s_{W,j}$ |
| `between_per_node.csv` | one per cell × metric × node | Per-node log-mean $\nu_i$, geomean $G^{\mathrm{node}}_i = e^{\nu_i}$, across-seed variance $s^{2}_{B,i}$ and $s_{B,i}$ |
| `summary.md` | this file | Equations, CSV guide, median summaries and conclusions across cells |

## Notation

Canonical symbols: `statistical_analysis/full_paper/analysis/NOTATION.md`. Fix one design cell and one metric $\chi$. Index **nodes** by $i = 1,\ldots,N_x$ ($N_x = 101$) and **seeds** by $j = 1,\ldots,N_s$ ($N_s = 100$). Work on the log scale

$$
Y_{ij} = \ln \chi_{ij}.
$$

All sums below are over finite $Y_{ij}$ only. Population (ddof = 0) means and variances divide by the count of terms (not $N_x-1$).

### Central tendency

**Seed log-mean** (average across nodes at fixed seed) and **seed geomean**:

$$
\mu_j = \frac{1}{N_x}\sum_{i=1}^{N_x} Y_{ij},\qquad G^{\mathrm{seed}}_j = e^{\mu_j}.
$$

**Node log-mean** (average across seeds at fixed node) and **node geomean**:

$$
\nu_i = \frac{1}{N_s}\sum_{j=1}^{N_s} Y_{ij},\qquad G^{\mathrm{node}}_i = e^{\nu_i}.
$$

**Overall log-mean** and **overall geomean** (CSV: `ln_chi_bar`, `chi_geom`):

$$
\bar{Y} = \frac{1}{N_x N_s}\sum_{i=1}^{N_x}\sum_{j=1}^{N_s} Y_{ij},\qquad G = e^{\bar{Y}}.
$$

On a complete balanced grid,

$$
G =\Bigl(\prod_{j=1}^{N_s} G^{\mathrm{seed}}_j\Bigr)^{1/N_s} =\Bigl(\prod_{i=1}^{N_x} G^{\mathrm{node}}_i\Bigr)^{1/N_x}.
$$

Also reported in `cell_summary.csv`:

- Arithmetic mean: $\overline{\chi} = \mathrm{mean}_{ij}(\chi_{ij})$ (`chi_mean`)
- Median: $\mathrm{median}_{ij}(\chi_{ij})$ (`chi_median`)
- Percentiles of seed/node geomeans: $G^{\mathrm{seed}}_{P10}, G^{\mathrm{seed}}_{P90}$, $G^{\mathrm{node}}_{P10}, G^{\mathrm{node}}_{P90}$

### Within-seed and across-seed conditional variances

**Within-seed** variance (node scatter at fixed seed $j$):

$$
s^{2}_{W,j} =\frac{1}{N_x}\sum_{i=1}^{N_x} (Y_{ij} - \mu_j)^2.
$$

Design-level summary (average over seeds; CSV rms form `s_W_bar` $= \sqrt{\overline{s^{2}_W}}$):

$$
\overline{s^{2}_W} =\frac{1}{N_s}\sum_{j=1}^{N_s} s^{2}_{W,j}.
$$

**Across-seed** variance at fixed node $i$ (seed-to-seed scatter at one depth):

$$
s^{2}_{B,i} =\frac{1}{N_s}\sum_{j=1}^{N_s} (Y_{ij} - \nu_i)^2.
$$

Design-level summary (average over nodes; CSV `s_B_bar`):

$$
\overline{s^{2}_B} =\frac{1}{N_x}\sum_{i=1}^{N_x} s^{2}_{B,i}.
$$

### Law of total variance (primary splits)

**Direct total variance** of all log entries (CSV `s_total` $= \sqrt{\sigma^{2}_{\mathrm{total}}}$):

$$
\sigma^{2}_{\mathrm{total}} =\frac{1}{N_x N_s}\sum_{i=1}^{N_x}\sum_{j=1}^{N_s} (Y_{ij} - \bar{Y})^2.
$$

**Variance of seed means** (CSV `s_mu` $= \sqrt{\sigma^{2}_{\mu}}$):

$$
\sigma^{2}_{\mu} =\frac{1}{N_s}\sum_{j=1}^{N_s} (\mu_j - \bar{Y})^2.
$$

**Variance of node means** (CSV `s_nu` $= \sqrt{\sigma^{2}_{\nu}}$):

$$
\sigma^{2}_{\nu} =\frac{1}{N_x}\sum_{i=1}^{N_x} (\nu_i - \bar{Y})^2.
$$

**Seed-conditioned decomposition** (within a realization vs across realizations):

$$
\sigma^{2}_{\mathrm{total}}= \overline{s^{2}_W} + \sigma^{2}_{\mu}.
$$

**Node-conditioned decomposition** (seed noise at a depth vs depth-to-depth structure):

$$
\sigma^{2}_{\mathrm{total}}= \overline{s^{2}_B} + \sigma^{2}_{\nu}.
$$

Both identities hold (up to floating point) on a complete grid; `decomp_ok` is `True` when both reconstructions match $\sigma^{2}_{\mathrm{total}}$.

### Fractions

$$
f_{W\mid\mathrm{seed}} =\frac{\overline{s^{2}_W}}{\sigma^{2}_{\mathrm{total}}},\qquad f_{\mu} =\frac{\sigma^{2}_{\mu}}{\sigma^{2}_{\mathrm{total}}},
$$

$$
f_{B\mid\mathrm{node}} =\frac{\overline{s^{2}_B}}{\sigma^{2}_{\mathrm{total}}},\qquad f_{\nu} =\frac{\sigma^{2}_{\nu}}{\sigma^{2}_{\mathrm{total}}}.
$$

CSV columns: `frac_W_seed`, `frac_mu`, `frac_B_node`, `frac_nu`. Within each split the two fractions sum to 1.

### Naive sum (diagnostic only)

Averaging the two conditional variances and adding them does **not** recover $\sigma^{2}_{\mathrm{total}}$ in general:

$$
s^{2}_{T,\mathrm{naive}}= \overline{s^{2}_W} + \overline{s^{2}_B},\qquad s_{T,\mathrm{naive}} = \sqrt{s^{2}_{T,\mathrm{naive}}}.
$$

$$
s_{T,\mathrm{gap}}= s_{T,\mathrm{naive}} - s_{\mathrm{total}}.
$$

CSV: `s_T_naive`, `s_T_gap`. Prefer the law-of-total-variance fractions above for interpretation.

### Interaction residual

Additive two-way fit residual

$$
R_{ij} = Y_{ij} - \mu_j - \nu_i + \bar{Y},
$$

with $\sigma^{2}_{R} = \mathrm{Var}_{ij}(R_{ij})$ (CSV `s_interaction` $= \sqrt{\sigma^{2}_{R}}$, `frac_interaction` $= \sigma^{2}_{R}/\sigma^{2}_{\mathrm{total}}$). Large $f_R$ flags seed×node structure beyond additive main effects.

### Dominance ratios

$$
\frac{\overline{s^{2}_W}}{\sigma^{2}_{\mu}}\quad(\texttt{ratio\_W\_over\_mu}),\qquad \frac{\overline{s^{2}_B}}{\sigma^{2}_{\nu}}\quad(\texttt{ratio\_B\_over\_nu}).
$$

## Per-metric medians across cells

| Metric | median $G$ | median $s_{\mathrm{total}}$ | median $f_\mu$ | median $f_W$ | median $f_\nu$ | median $f_B$ | decomp_ok |
|--------|---------:|---------------:|--------------:|--------------:|--------------:|--------------:|----------:|
| f_ratio | 0.9731 | 0.0377 | 0.805 | 0.195 | 0.002 | 0.998 | 243 / 243 |
| abs_TF_ratio | 0.1245 | 0.5143 | 0.886 | 0.114 | 0.001 | 0.999 | 243 / 243 |
| PGA_ratio | 0.8818 | 0.1308 | 0.174 | 0.826 | 0.010 | 0.990 | 243 / 243 |
| PSA_ratio | 0.8222 | 0.1435 | 0.195 | 0.805 | 0.010 | 0.990 | 243 / 243 |
| Ia_ratio | 0.6479 | 0.3209 | 0.180 | 0.820 | 0.012 | 0.988 | 243 / 243 |

## Conclusions

- **`f_ratio`**: median geomean $G \approx 0.9731$, median $\sigma_{\ln} \approx 0.0377$. Seed-conditioned variability is dominated by seed-to-seed shifts of the depth-averaged level ($f_\mu=0.80 \ge f_W=0.20$). Node-conditioned variability is dominated by seed noise at fixed depth ($f_B=1.00 \ge f_\nu=0.00$).
- **`abs_TF_ratio`**: median geomean $G \approx 0.1245$, median $\sigma_{\ln} \approx 0.5143$. Seed-conditioned variability is dominated by seed-to-seed shifts of the depth-averaged level ($f_\mu=0.89 \ge f_W=0.11$). Node-conditioned variability is dominated by seed noise at fixed depth ($f_B=1.00 \ge f_\nu=0.00$).
- **`PGA_ratio`**: median geomean $G \approx 0.8818$, median $\sigma_{\ln} \approx 0.1308$. Seed-conditioned variability is dominated by within-seed depth scatter ($f_W=0.83 > f_\mu=0.17$). Node-conditioned variability is dominated by seed noise at fixed depth ($f_B=0.99 \ge f_\nu=0.01$).
- **`PSA_ratio`**: median geomean $G \approx 0.8222$, median $\sigma_{\ln} \approx 0.1435$. Seed-conditioned variability is dominated by within-seed depth scatter ($f_W=0.81 > f_\mu=0.19$). Node-conditioned variability is dominated by seed noise at fixed depth ($f_B=0.99 \ge f_\nu=0.01$).
- **`Ia_ratio`**: median geomean $G \approx 0.6479$, median $\sigma_{\ln} \approx 0.3209$. Seed-conditioned variability is dominated by within-seed depth scatter ($f_W=0.82 > f_\mu=0.18$). Node-conditioned variability is dominated by seed noise at fixed depth ($f_B=0.99 \ge f_\nu=0.01$).

